index 4479b53..aec8705 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -15,3 +15,25 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Passkeys and account security
+
+Requires Node.js 24 or newer. Password registration and verification continue to use the existing Times authentication service; passwords are not stored locally. After creating an account, sign in and visit **Account security** to register a passkey. Returning readers can sign in with the passkey button or supported username autofill. Account security supports multiple passkeys, security keys, nicknames, creation/last-use dates, deletion, display-name changes, and sign-out.
+
+Sensitive changes require password verification within the last five minutes or passkey reauthentication with device PIN/biometrics. Reauthentication only accepts the signed-in account's passkeys. Password sign-in remains available if a passkey is lost or the last passkey is deleted.
+
+For production, configure runtime environment variables:
+
+```sh
+WEBAUTHN_ORIGIN=https://your-site.example
+WEBAUTHN_RP_ID=your-site.example
+AUTH_DB_PATH=/persistent-volume/auth.sqlite
+```
+
+`WEBAUTHN_ORIGIN` is the exact public origin, including a non-default port when applicable, without a path or trailing slash. `WEBAUTHN_RP_ID` defaults to that origin's hostname. HTTPS is required in production. Localhost development automatically uses the request origin. Passkeys belong to the RP domain, so changing it requires registering new passkeys. The app's `/devtools-times/` base path is preserved.
+
+Users, public credentials, hashed session tokens, and expiring challenges are persisted in SQLite (default `.data/auth.sqlite`). Mount a durable volume and back it up. This storage supports a single deployment with shared local SQLite access; independently scaled instances need a shared transactional database implementation. Never deploy with ephemeral credential storage. Session cookies are HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax, scoped to the app base path, and Secure on HTTPS. The original password service must remain available for password sign-in, signup, and password reauthentication. Passkey authentication works independently after enrollment.
+
+Provider names are sourced from the [passkey AAGUID registry](https://github.com/passkeydeveloper/passkey-authenticator-aaguids) and used only as display hints. Password-manager synchronization is best effort on browsers that support WebAuthn Signal methods. Older supported WebAuthn browsers receive JSON/capability polyfills; unsupported browsers retain password access.
+
+Run `pnpm test` to build and run the HTTP integration suite. The tests generate an authenticator keypair and sign real WebAuthn assertions without opening a browser or contacting the external password service. They cover registration, authentication, challenge replay/expiry, signature and counter failures, origin/session boundaries, reauthentication ownership/user verification, management authorization, and logout.
